Package: mouthtype-linux
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: CodesWhat <80784472+scttbnsn@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-jeepney, curl, pipewire-audio, libnotify-bin, ffmpeg
Recommends: wl-clipboard, wtype, hyprland | sway
Suggests: quickshell, mouthtype-linux-desktop
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://mouthtype.app/linux/
Description: local voice dictation client for Wayland desktops
 Mouthtype records on a hotkey, transcribes on this machine with a pinned
 speech model and delivers the text to the focused window. Nothing leaves the
 computer.
 .
 This package installs the client, the Omarchy bar plugin sources and a
 systemd user units. It downloads no model and enables no service. After
 installing, run "mouthtype-linux-setup" as your normal user to fetch the
 speech model (about 465 MiB) and enable the per-user service.
 .
 Development client for Linux x86_64. On Hyprland, paste and type delivery use
 wl-clipboard and wtype. The bar plugin needs Quickshell, which Debian and
 Ubuntu do not package, so it is only listed as a suggestion. GNOME and KDE
 Plasma sessions also need the mouthtype-linux-desktop package, which adds the
 settings window and tray icon and does not pull PySide6 onto other desktops.
